## 4. Slice summary

The substantive formulas in Q6 pass the requested algebraic hazard test: they use finite residue fields, integer Bézout/grid arithmetic, Newton-polygon data, unit characters, and henselian-style residual constructions. I found no use of characteristic-zero Taylor expansions, \(v(p)<\infty\), odd-prime tests, Teichmüller/Witt machinery, or unjustified roots/division; separability is either explicitly assumed for the input polynomial or used only for residual polynomials over perfect finite fields. Nevertheless, the notes do **not already prove** uniformity across every complete DVR with residue size \(q\). The decisive failure is H6 plus domain restriction: the load-bearing GMN print is documented here as mixed-characteristic, JA-PIN only treats \(\mathbb Z_p\) and \(\mathbf F_p[[t]]\), and equal-characteristic rows are explicitly machine-only/“no PARI leg.” Thus the evidence strongly suggests the extension needs no new combinatorial idea, but a published-scope replacement or a fresh general henselian-DVR proof is still required.

